# ==============================================================================
# THE PDF THIS PROJECT BUILDS (the pandoc pack)
# ==============================================================================
# What `gmake pdf` reads. `gmake env_project_enable` copies this block into the
# project's .env the first time it runs; after that it only adds what is
# missing, so a value you filled in is never overwritten.
#
# All three are optional: a project with one markdown file and the template
# called template.tex says nothing here, and the target finds everything. The
# lines stay commented out on purpose - a commented line does not travel into
# the .env, and leaving it out means "unset, and the target decides".
#
# Nothing reads this file: it is a sample. The project's .env is what gmake
# loads.
# ==============================================================================

# --- The markdown to build, when the project holds several ---
# Example: PDF_SRC=rapport.md
#PDF_SRC=

# --- What to write, when the derived name is not the one you want ---
# Example: PDF_OUT=rapport-rv.pdf
#PDF_OUT=

# --- The template, when the project's is not template.tex ---
# Example: PDF_TEMPLATE=templates/rapport.tex
#PDF_TEMPLATE=
